---
import AboutPoster from '../assets/about-poster.webp';
import HeroMedia from '../components/HeroMedia.astro';
import { SOCIAL_LINKS } from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="About Ayushman Malla — hardware engineer exploring FPGA design, high-level synthesis, digital verification, and applied AI."
	mainClass="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6"
>
	<section class="py-10 sm:py-14">
		<p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-accent uppercase">
			<span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-[2px] bg-accent" />
			<span>About</span>
		</p>
		<h1 class="heading-page mt-3 font-bold text-foreground">About Me</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:text-lg">
			Hardware engineer thinking at the intersection of computing, verification, and intelligence.
		</p>

		<div class="my-8">
			<HeroMedia
				image={AboutPoster}
				video="/media/about.mp4"
				alt="Kinetic typography header for About Ayushman Malla"
				aspectClass="aspect-[16/9]"
				class="rounded-2xl border border-border"
				priority={true}
			/>
		</div>

		<div class="mb-8 flex items-center gap-3" aria-hidden="true">
			<span class="h-[2px] w-12 bg-accent" />
			<span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border" />
		</div>

		<div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-[1.75] text-foreground/85 sm:text-lg">
			<p>
				Hi, I’m Ayushman Malla — a hardware engineer and builder who enjoys thinking at the intersection of computing, design, and intelligence. I’m currently exploring how abstraction, verification, and synthesis shape the boundary between algorithms and silicon. My work revolves around FPGA design, high-level synthesis (HLS), and digital verification, with a deep curiosity about how hardware can be reimagined for AI and high-performance systems.
			</p>
			<p>
				Recently, I worked at Transcelestial as an FPGA/Hardware Engineering Intern, developing a 10G Ethernet packet forwarder on Xilinx Zynq UltraScale+ MPSoC, following an internship at AMD debugging EPYC CPU memory subsystems. Beyond hardware, I’ve built AI/ML projects ranging from financial analytics tools to deep learning models for medical imaging and autonomous vehicles — enjoying the full stack from transistor logic to inference runtime.
			</p>
			<p>
				Outside of engineering, I find satisfaction in solving math puzzles (for some reason I am obsessed with Rubik’s cubes), watching people cook, and playing tennis. I value precision, iteration, and clarity of thought — qualities that guide how I approach both design problems and life in general.
			</p>
			<p>
				I’m also fascinated by meta-cognition: how people structure knowledge, synthesize abstractions, and turn insight into execution. This portfolio is a space where I share my projects, reflections, and ideas — from technical breakdowns to thought experiments. At its core, it’s a record of one ongoing pursuit: to build systems, and ways of thinking, that scale.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 sm:p-6">
			<p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-accent uppercase">Connect</p>
			<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2.5 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm">
				<a
					href={SOCIAL_LINKS.email}
					class="text-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"
				>
					{SOCIAL_LINKS.emailDisplay}
				</a>
				<a
					href={SOCIAL_LINKS.github}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"
				>
					GitHub ↗
				</a>
				<a
					href={SOCIAL_LINKS.linkedin}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"
				>
					LinkedIn ↗
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
